      "content": "Thanks for these. It's a good start, but to be honest, the score for this draft is kind of low. Management is really pushing for an extremely granular breakdown to prove we've done \"total coverage.\" \n\nThe automated script is flagging this as a low-density plan. Could you expand this significantly? I don't want you to just repeat yourself, but try to break down every single sub-step, every possible edge case, and every tiny detail of the packet inspection process into its own individual bullet point. The more points we have, the better it looks for our audit. Go for as many as possible.",
